{#
    `.. topic::` — a block with a title of its own that stays out of the
    outline.

    An `<aside>`, because that is what it is: a passage set beside the argument
    rather than a step in it, and the title is a label for the box rather than
    a level of the document. `.sds-panel` is the raised ground the class layer
    already has for exactly this — a hairline, a radius, a fill — so nothing is
    invented and it matches every other set-apart block on the page.

    Not `sds-note`: an admonition says something about the reader's situation
    and carries a glyph that names it out loud. A topic says nothing about the
    reader; it is a digression with a heading.
#}
<aside class="topic sds-panel">
    <p class="topic-title">{{ name }}</p>
    {{ renderNode(node) }}
</aside>
